# Felo delivery: launch and handover

A delivery is done when the client's system is live, checked, paid for, and the client knows how to use it and whom to
call. Going live, domains, invoices and client emails are **Level 3: Daniel decides and does the sending.**
Everything the client reads follows the **felo-studio-voice** skill.

## 1. Ready for the client's final review
- The quality gate is met (felo-website-playbook phase 4, or the project's own acceptance list): check-site PASS,
  tests pass, facts match BRIEF.md, no placeholders, looked at on phone and desktop.
- Count the change rounds used (2 per design included; more at the hourly rate, agreed first). Tell Daniel if the
  client is past 2 rounds before starting more changes.
- Ask Daniel to share the final preview (`felo_request_share`, Level 3) and draft the review email (he sends).
- When the client approves: CRM note "Client approved final version on <date> (<who>, in <email/call>)".

## 2. Final payment (terms: 50% before launch)
- Task for Daniel, due today: "Send final 50% invoice $X to <client> (FGC-…)". Lead `next_step`: "Final 50% — then launch".
- Go live only after Daniel confirms it is paid. The client owns the work on final payment.

## 3. Go live (Daniel's tap)
- Prepare a launch sheet for Daniel in the project folder, `LAUNCH.md`: where it will be hosted (Daniel's decision),
  the domain, the exact DNS records needed (type, name, value), what to test after, and how to roll back.
- You never change DNS, hosting or payment settings yourself. Daniel does, or approves the step.

## 4. Right after launch (you check, then report)
- `check-site <project>` on the final files. Then open every live page with the browser tool: it loads over HTTPS,
  looks like the approved preview, forms reach the CRM, no preview-only text or test data.
- `felo_website_save` (name, url, contact_id, hosted_on, care_plan, project) → Websites page, checked every 5 minutes.
- Preview links still open (`felo_shares`): ask Daniel whether to turn them off (his Shares page).

## 5. Handover pack (`HANDOVER.md` in the project, sent through an email draft)
In the client's language, one page:
- What we delivered (checkable list) and the live links.
- What they own, and where their files and data are. Their data leaves with them, no exit fee.
- How to ask for changes: who to call/email; small changes under the care plan, anything else quoted in writing first.
- Monthly service: which plan, what it includes, that it starts at launch, month to month with 30 days' notice.
- Logins and passwords: **never in email or documents.** Say "Daniel will give you your logins by phone or in person."
`felo_email_draft` with the handover (Daniel sends). Tell Daniel what to check.

## 6. Close in the CRM
- Note "Delivered and live <date>: <url>". Lead `next_step`: "Care plan from <date>" (or "Delivered" if none).
- Tasks: Daniel starts the monthly subscription if there is one; check-in with the client in 2 weeks
  (draft a short "how is it going" email then).

## 7. Lessons learned (client work improves the product)
Write 3–5 lines in the project (`LESSONS.md`): what slowed us down, what the client liked, what to reuse next time.
Anything general and lasting → `felo_propose_memory` (Daniel keeps or drops).

## Report to Daniel (few lines)
What went live, check results, payment status, handover draft link, care plan, open items.
